Dialogue: 2,0:01:49.78,0:01:54.86,Title-207-,,0,0,0,,{\blur0.5\fad(725,0)\c&HE7E6E5&\bord0\4a&HFF&}Noland the Liar
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.59,0:01:57.41,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I can't believe our luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.41,0:02:00.97,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Seriously, that orangutan almost sunk us.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.33,0:02:04.91,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,And now it's up to me to fix it\Nall and keep this thing afloat.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.99,0:02:08.01,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Seems to me that this busted\Nold ship is on our last leg.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.09,0:02:09.09,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,We need a new one.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.17,0:02:11.63,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,How dare you even consider\Nreplacing this boat?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.71,0:02:12.81,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Yeah, how dare you?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.89,0:02:14.35,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,We all know the story, Usopp.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.43,0:02:16.25,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,And try not to be so defensive.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.55,0:02:18.95,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,The going mare is an\Nimportant part of our crew,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.03,0:02:20.97,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,and we all know we have\Nto take care of her.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.05,0:02:23.33,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,You shouldn't take\Neverything so personally.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.41,0:02:24.24,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.33,0:02:25.23,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.83,0:02:28.66,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Oops.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.79,0:02:34.63,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,We left Mocktown and\Nheaded east by circling
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.71,0:02:36.33,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,around the northern shore of the island.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.41,0:02:38.31,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Our destination is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.49,0:02:40.15,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,We're supposed to meet that man there.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.23,0:02:41.06,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,What's his name?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.14,0:02:42.53,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,His name is Mockblot Cricket.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.61,0:02:45.96,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,And you're sure that he'll be\Nable to help us out, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.33,0:02:48.29,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Whoa! Amazing!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.85,0:02:51.14,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,That's where he lives?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.29,0:02:52.71,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,It's a freaking palace!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.03,0:02:55.09,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I've never seen a house that big before!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.17,0:02:58.11,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,This Mont Blanc cricket\Nguy must be really loaded!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.69,0:02:59.63,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Look closer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.83,0:03:01.30,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,It's really unattractive.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.55,0:03:05.37,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,A guy's got to have some serious\Nguts to build a house that ugly.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.75,0:03:06.61,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.49,0:03:14.01,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,This isn't a palace at all! What?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.43,0:03:16.71,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,The actual house is only half that size.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.79,0:03:18.61,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,What you see is a facade, a fake.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.69,0:03:20.87,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,This guy's even more vain than I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.95,0:03:24.51,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Why exactly did Cricket decide to\Nleave his home and come live here?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.59,0:03:26.30,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I don't know all the details,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.65,0:03:28.93,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,but I think it has something\Nto do with his belief.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.01,0:03:31.85,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,that a large amount of gold rests\Nsomewhere in the hills of Jaya.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.93,0:03:32.76,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Gold?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.84,0:03:34.85,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Do you think he's here searching\Nfor some sort of buried treasure?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.93,0:03:37.15,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Well, I just don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.01,0:03:38.84,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.75,0:03:41.21,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Try over here, Chopper.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.37,0:03:42.39,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Take out this spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.47,0:03:44.00,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I'll be right there, Nami.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.25,0:03:46.95,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Must be hard to live alone\Nin such a remote area.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.03,0:03:47.86,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Hello!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.05,0:03:49.58,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Don't just barge in there!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.07,0:03:51.84,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Huh, looks like nobody's home.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.03,0:03:53.01,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Anybody here?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.01,0:03:55.33,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I guess he's gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.63,0:03:56.73,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Get out of there, you idiot.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.81,0:03:58.37,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,This guy could be dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.45,0:03:59.63,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Hey, you guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.97,0:04:00.89,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Nobody's home.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.89,0:04:03.73,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Huh, what's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.01,0:04:06.84,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,A book?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.92,0:04:08.51,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,And it looks pretty old.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.05,0:04:09.88,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.96,0:04:11.65,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,It's called Noland the Liar.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.67,0:04:13.50,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.58,0:04:14.93,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Sounds like it could be good.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.01,0:04:16.30,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I sure like the title.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.85,0:04:19.41,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Nolan the Liar? Yeah.\NHave you heard of it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.65,0:04:23.23,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,It says here it was originally\Npublished in the North Blue Territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.31,0:04:24.14,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,It was.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.22,0:04:25.99,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I was born in the North Blue Territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.07,0:04:28.23,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I'm certain I must have\Ntold you guys that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.31,0:04:29.14,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,No?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.22,0:04:30.05,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,That's news to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.14,0:04:31.37,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I always thought you\Nwere born in the East.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.45,0:04:32.29,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I grew up there.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.37,0:04:33.53,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Enough already, Chopper.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.61,0:04:34.73,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.37,0:04:38.85,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Where I come from, this is a famous story.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.11,0:04:42.41,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,It's a fairy tale supposedly\Nbased on the life of Noland.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.49,0:04:45.08,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,who lived in the North\NBlue a long time ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.93,0:04:50.57,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,This is a story of ancient origins.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.95,0:04:54.61,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,The events herein transpired\Nmore than 400 years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.43,0:04:58.83,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,There once was a man by the\Nname of Montblanc Noland,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.03,0:05:01.38,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,who lived in the North Blue countryside.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.93,0:05:03.61,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Noland, who was an explorer,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.11,0:05:07.85,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,always regaled the crowds with\Nstories of his incredible exploits,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.93,0:05:11.99,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,but nobody knew whether or not to\Ntake Noland's tall tales seriously.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.59,0:05:15.59,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,One day, upon returning\Nfrom yet another adventure,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.83,0:05:18.29,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,he reported to his king\Nall that he had seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.37,0:05:22.55,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,I saw a city of gold on an island\Nin the Great Sea, declared Noland.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.71,0:05:27.42,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,and the courageous king decided that he\Nmust have this treasure for his kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.81,0:05:32.63,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,The king set out with Noland and 2,000\Nof his finest soldiers. Along the way,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.71,0:05:36.85,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,they endured treacherous storms and\Nbattled many ferocious sea creatures.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.93,0:05:38.57,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,At the end of their journey,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.65,0:05:40.03,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,only the king, Noland,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.19,0:05:44.81,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,and 100 soldiers survived to set foot on\Nthe island that housed the City of Gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.89,0:05:46.93,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,And all they found for\Ntheir troubles was a
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.01,0:05:49.72,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,normal island covered\Nwith an ordinary jungle.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.99,0:05:51.51,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,And so upon their return,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.81,0:05:55.31,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,Noland was sentenced to death for\Nthe crime of lying to his king.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.39,0:05:59.41,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,His last words were as\Nfollows: I can only assume
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.49,0:06:02.35,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,that the city of gold\Nsunk into the sea the
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.43,0:06:05.07,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,king and his court were\Ndumbfounded nobody believed
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.15,0:06:07.55,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,in Oland anymore and the\Nlast of his days were
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.63,0:06:10.05,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,spent in shame and ridicule\Nbefore his sentence
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.13,0:06:12.53,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,of death was carried out\Nbefore a cheering crowd
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.61,0:06:15.35,Dubtitles,,0,0,0,,it says here that the\Nbook is based on the true
